// DRC runset for Calibre, SMIC 0.18 (smic18ee), cell DSH_NMOS/dsh_nmos2
//
// Why a runset instead of the deck's own defaults: the shipped deck hardcodes
//     LAYOUT PATH "xxx.gds" / DRC RESULTS DATABASE "drc_cal.out"
// so the three lines that say WHAT to check are all placeholders. Overriding
// them here means the deck file itself stays untouched (it is foundry material,
// and edits to it would make every later run unreproducible).
//
// The input is GDS, not the OA database: Calibre reads GDSII. So the flow is
// streamOut -> calibre -drc -> parse. That round trip also proves the layout
// really is in the database with the layers we think it has, rather than only
// appearing so in the editor.

// ---- what to check ---------------------------------------------------------
LAYOUT PATH "/tmp/drc/dsh_nmos2.gds"
LAYOUT PRIMARY "dsh_nmos2"
LAYOUT SYSTEM GDSII

DRC RESULTS DATABASE "/tmp/drc/dsh_nmos2.drc.results" ASCII
DRC SUMMARY REPORT    "/tmp/drc/dsh_nmos2.drc.summary"

// Keep going after the first error so one run yields the whole picture.
DRC MAXIMUM RESULTS 1000
DRC MAXIMUM VERTEX 4096

// Threads: the guest has few cores; requesting more than exist only adds
// scheduling noise to the timing numbers.
DRC NUM THREADS 2
